{
  "outcome": "pending_approval",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi Tom, sorry about the timing with month-end close. I've looked into it. Your account was locked after several wrong-password attempts this morning. They all came from the office network during your normal hours, so nothing looks suspicious. I've asked a technician to unlock your account, and you'll be able to sign in again as soon as they approve it. This morning you signed in successfully once, then the failures started again, which usually means a device somewhere is still trying an old saved password. Before or right after you're unlocked, please check your phone's mail app, Teams on your phone, and any other computer or tablet, and update or re-enter your password on each one. Otherwise the account may lock again. If you don't remember your current password, reply and we'll set up a reset. The temporary password would be given to you by phone. If it locks again after you've updated your devices, let us know right away.",
  "internal_note": "Checked the account: status is locked (not disabled), 5 failed logins, MFA not the issue, sign-in not blocked, password last set 2026-07-23, must_change_password=false. Sign-in logs: all 5 failures were on 2026-10-09 between 09:20 and 09:35 ET from corporate IP 203.0.113.10 (New York), within usual hours. There was a successful Duo-push sign-in at 09:28, then 3 more failures after it. That pattern points to a device with an old saved password (probably the phone mail app) or mistyping. No hosting networks or foreign locations, so KB-031 doesn't apply. The request came from the user's own verified email. Unlock is queued (approval id 1). I did not request a password reset because the user didn't say they forgot it. If they do, follow KB-001 step 2. Per KB-001, escalate if it locks again within an hour after saved passwords are updated.",
  "kb_articles": [
    "KB-001"
  ],
  "confidence": "high"
}
